# API key route access

Keys are default-deny. A route accepts a key only when `ensureAuthenticated` or
`optionalEnsureAuthenticated` carries `apiKeyAccess: { resource, action }`. A
`rateLimitAuthEndpoint` wrapper that authenticates first carries the same requirement.

The resource is the account data the route reads or changes (`API_KEY_RESOURCES`). A path under one
prefix can belong to another resource: followed-playlist lists are `subscriptions`, and subscribed
lists under `/channel`, `/item`, `/live-item`, `/clip`, and `/account` are `subscriptions`.

The action follows HTTP intent. `GET`, and a `POST` that only reads, are `read`. A `POST` that adds
a row is `create` (follow, add to a playlist or any queue zone including history, enqueue a feed
parse). `PATCH`, `PUT`, and a `POST` that changes existing state (mark read, mark seen, toggle,
reorder, promote, replay, bulk enable or disable, hide or unhide) are `update`. `DELETE`, and a
`POST` that removes rows (unfollow), are `delete`. Settings writes are all `update`; the settings
row always exists. Routes sharing one rate-limit wrapper share one requirement.

Never add `apiKeyAccess` to API key management, sessions, password, email change, account deletion,
the data export, terms acceptance, the listen-stats consent and its agreement text, listen and open
reports (`POST /stats/listen`, `POST /stats/open`), billing, membership claim tokens, or minting
MetaBoost app assertions.

The action must be one `apiKeyResourceSupportsAction` allows. A route for an action the list omits
adds that action to `API_KEY_SUPPORTED_ACTIONS` in the same change.

With a new or changed authenticated route, in the same change: set or deliberately omit
`apiKeyAccess`; add or update `x-api-key-permission` and the `apiKeyAuth` security entry in
`apps/api/openapi.yml` (or keep both off for a closed route); add the route to the matching
`apps/api/src/test/api-key-routes-*.integration.test.ts` table.

Related: **openapi-sync**, **api-testing**.
